{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\n`tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py` was introduced by the `d6669496..88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684` delta and has no recorded file-impact owner. At `origin/main@88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684` it contains exactly four editable blocks: three true leading docstrings and one full-line comment region, 461 before-words. Counts use `(?u)\\b[^\\W_]\\w*(?:[-'][^\\W_]\\w*)*\\b`.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\n- `D:<module>@1-32[316]` — retain the two-root hazard and why static plus dynamic enforcement are both required; remove chronology, lane history, uppercase narration, and duplication.\n- `C:<module>:before:_ALLOWED@52-55[49]` — retain why the production-resolver test is the sole safe exception.\n- `D:test_no_test_module_resolves_the_installed_engine_root@80-85[44]` — retain checkout-root and AST false-positive behavior.\n- `D:split_engine@138-143[52]` — retain the install-mode-independent split fixture contract.\n\n## Consumers and protected prose\nThe module is a direct pytest input and pins `tests/_engine_path.py` plus the root-conftest guard. Preserve the static scanner, allowlist anti-drift assertion, manufactured foreign-root topology, canonical/shadow controls, and all runtime strings/assertions.\n\nAll unlisted prose is protected as concise or load-bearing: lines 48-49; `_installed_root_sites`, `test_the_conftest_guard_is_wired_to_the_detector`, the foreign-`__path__` test, and the canonical-shadow test docstrings; the line-146 `__pycache__` comment; and every other one-line helper/test docstring.\n\n## Preservation and review contract\nCompare immutable `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:<path>` blobs with the final commit. Parse Python with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`; remove only the allowlisted leading owner docstrings; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining AST to match. Reject changes to inline or non-allowlisted comments. Preserve runtime strings, assertions, decorators, test data, shebangs, and every directive-bearing physical line exactly. Only adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the leaf must post exactly 4 leaf-linked TSV rows:\n`stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\nBefore citations use `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:<path>#<stable-id>`; final citations use `<full-final-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>`. Every row must have `after_words < before_words` and all three verdict fields PASS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The one-commit changed-path set is exactly the 1-path file-impact set.\n- [ ] Only the 4 declared prose blocks and adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] The normalized non-docstring AST remains identical.\n- [ ] Every runtime string remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every non-allowlisted comment remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every directive-bearing physical line remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every directive remains attached to the same statement.\n- [ ] Every shebang remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV contains exactly 4 rows.\n- [ ] Every TSV row has an immutable-base citation.\n- [ ] Every TSV row has a full-final-SHA citation.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `after_words < before_words`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `directives_exact=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every recorded content/AST verification command exits 0 at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] The recorded no-timeout worktree-venv `make verify` exits 0 at the leaf commit.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788667673701560001,"uuid":"f53068e0-9295-4825-a772-529cb7b12bab"}